{%- comment -%} Mirrors "Sous stays second in command" (Control) in site/index.html. Keep the copy identical to that file. {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="bg-paper" aria-label="Control">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head head--idx"><div class="head-body">
      <h2 class="display">Sous stays <em>second in command.</em></h2>
    </div></div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>A good sous chef follows someone else's recipe, does their part well and makes it easy to repeat, without ever making the dish their own.</p>
      <p>That's how it works here. You choose the tea, set the recipe and decide what the finished cup should be.</p>
      <p>Sous is only as good as the matcha you use and the choices you make. It gets you as close as you can get to your own best cup.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="presets">
      <article class="preset"><span class="pvol">3</span><h3>Saved settings</h3><p>Save different settings for your mood or your matcha, ready at the touch of a button.</p></article>
      <article class="preset"><span class="pvol">18</span><h3>Speeds</h3><p>Adjust the movement for your matcha and the texture you prefer.</p></article>
      <article class="preset"><span class="pvol">40&thinsp;&middot;&thinsp;80&thinsp;&middot;&thinsp;120</span><h3>Etched guides</h3><p>Fill to the line that matches your recipe, so the same mood or matcha gets the same ratio every time.</p></article>
    </div>
    <figure class="wide-detail">
      <span class="media-frame"><img src="{{ 'tile-measures-v3.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="The etched 40, 80 and 120 ml guides and the mixing whisk inside the stainless mixing cup" width="1200" height="1124" loading="lazy"></span>
      <figcaption>Etched 40 &middot; 80 &middot; 120 ml</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{ "name": "Second in command", "presets": [{ "name": "Second in command" }] }
{% endschema %}
